=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/LiveSignalInspector (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/LiveSignalInspector   kind=page   web route=/admin/live-signals
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/LiveSignalInspectorPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.826) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the data-port seam + Empty/client feeds), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's
  idealized "LiveSignalInspectorPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these
  real conventions (same precedent as the sibling W7 admin pages — see windows-page-admin-ApiLogsPage.log); the
  surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("LiveSignalInspector"). The
  RouteTable already maps Page("LiveSignalInspector","admin/live-signals",RouteGroup.AdminDevTools).
- The page composes the already-ported native LiveSignalsTable feature-view (the parity port of the web
  components/live-signal-inspector/LiveSignalsTable.tsx) for the GlassPanel3 snapshot, so the per-second live read
  (web useVehicleLiveSignals → GET /signals/{vehicleID}/live) and its own loading/empty/error/stale branches are
  owned by that surface (DRY — not re-implemented). The page's OWN data source is the fleet picker
  (web useVehicles → GET /vehicles), bound through the injected ILiveSignalInspectorFeed (default
  EmptyLiveSignalInspectorFeed resolves the empty fleet; LiveSignalInspectorClientFeed binds the generated
  client operation get_api_v1_vehicles, ADR-004). The vehicle label uses the shared VehicleLabels.Short rule
  (display_name → VIN → "Vehicle {id}"), matching the web option label verbatim.
- All 7 i18n keys already exist verbatim in Strings/en/Resources.resw (translation.admin.liveSignals.*); the
  surface resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names (no new catalog rows required).
- SI units N/A at this surface (no unit-bearing fields on the picker); the composed LiveSignalsTable applies the
  shared SI converters + the >2-minute freshness/staleness chip (ADR-013) at its display boundary.

